  "summary": "SDK with ping/HTTP primitives; no traced installer harm",
  "details": "Package ships an SDK/orchestrator with several files that reference curl, ping, GET, and POST primitives (bin/room-orchestrator-boot.js, src/sdk/RoomOrchestrator.js, src/sdk/ServerAPI.js, src/sharding/RegionRouter.js). The keyword co-occurrence matched by pattern rules is the normal shape of a room-orchestration/server-API SDK that performs readiness checks (ping), region routing, and HTTP requests to its own service endpoints. No traced code path reads installer-side secrets (env scraping, ~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser stores), no hardcoded attacker-controlled destination is bound to an install- or import-time network call, and no lifecycle hook fetches and executes remote content. The observed primitives are consistent with the package's declared purpose rather than exfiltration.",
